# THIRD-PARTY DOCUMENTATION IS NOT OURS TO REDISTRIBUTE.
#
# docs/ doubles as the working reference shelf for this project: Keithley's DMM6500 manuals and TSP app
# examples, and the two processor reference manuals the display and timing work was done against. They
# are what the measurements were made against and they are cited throughout the code, but they are
# vendor copyright and this repository is public -- so they stay local.
#
# Listed by vendor rather than by a blanket docs/*.txt rule, so a document WE write in docs/ is
# published by default instead of silently disappearing.

# Keithley
docs/DMM6500_*.txt
docs/DMM6500-*.txt
docs/DMM6500DisplayDoc.md
docs/Display API Command Reference.md
docs/Keithley_DMM6500_Notes-*.txt
docs/1KW-*.txt
docs/2000SCAN-*.txt
docs/K10SCAN_schematic.txt
docs/LowLevelHandbook_*.txt
docs/TSPAPP-*.txt
docs/TSPAPP_*.txt

# Processor reference manuals
docs/Arm-Cortex-M4-Processor-Datasheet.txt
docs/e300coreRM.txt
docs/MPC5125RM.txt

# THE WORKING LOG STAYS LOCAL. notes/ is a session-by-session engineering journal -- bench wiring, the
# instruments' addresses, this unit's serial number and calibration date, firmware quirks, what was
# tried and abandoned. It is the most useful directory in the project to whoever is holding the probe
# and the least useful to whoever is reading the code, and publishing it would put a lot of unreviewed
# detail about a specific bench on the open web. What a reader needs is in docs/.
notes/

# Build output: regenerable by re-running the harness, and it dates immediately.
out/

# Local tooling and OS noise
.claude/
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# DSP proposal work -- kept locally, deliberately not tracked
csrc/
docs/NATIVE-DSP-PROPOSAL.md
docs/NATIVE-DSP-PROPOSAL.pdf
tools/make_pdf.py
